primordialsoup-by-faemiyah for Debian
-------------------------------------

This is the standard (non-compo) version of the 4k intro, not the minimized
"party" version.

The sources are built with the USE_LD definition: the synth (ia32 assembly)
is not used, so the music is not generated at runtime. The intro loads the
precalculated music and the shaders from /usr/share/primordialsoup-by-faemiyah.

The upstream 37 MB floating-point WAV file is converted to FLAC (24 bits)
at build time to keep the data package small. The intro reads it directly
with libsndfile (patch 08_load-flac-with-libsndfile.patch); up to 0ddebs6,
the maintainer scripts converted it back to WAV at installation time.

I always prefer using the most basic binary format to ensure compatibility
with dh_shlibdeps, allowing it to accurately identify dependencies.

Forcing music generation might be possible, but exploring the ASM code
suggests a loss of cross-platform compilation.

Debian changes:
 * V-Sync is enabled (07_enable-vsync.patch).
 * The window can be resized, the picture keeps its 16:9 aspect ratio.
 * F toggles fullscreen, Escape quits.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

